      "writtenOn": "2023-01-05T22:33:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I intentionally renamed this to `wgsl`. In the follow up CL, this backend flag will only be allowed in SPIR-V when the `SPIRVDawnCompatMode` setting is enabled. Once the WGSL backend is complete, this setting will be removed. The following CL also makes this test invalid and removes it, since the two binding declaration variants for `sampler2D` that are demonstrated here won\u0027t be allowed in the same program (`vkSampler` would only be allowed in `SPIRVDawnCompatMode` and the `yuvSampler` declaration would be illegal in `SPIRVDawnCompatMode`).\n\nI made this distinction because I\u0027m not allowing the split texture+sampler syntax in Vulkan SPIR-V and this makes it explicit that it is a WGSL/Dawn specific allowance.\n\nI\u0027m somewhat considering renaming `spirv` to `vk` to make it clear that this refers to our usage of \"Vulkan SPIR-V\". We already named the GL backend flag `gl` instead of `glsl` since GLSL has so many variants but the one we\u0027re specifically concerned about is the OpenGL (ES) variant.\n\nI hope this makes sense. Please let me know if you have any thoughts or suggestions.",
      "parentUuid": "b27cfc67_3fad9e9c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 2,
        "endChar": 11
      },
